CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*expected expression, but got type.*$
^.*member designator index.*out of bounds.*$
--
C++20 qualified concept name as a template type-constraint
([temp.param]/4, [temp.names]).  A constrained parameter
`template <ns::Concept T>` (the libstdc++ iter_reference_t shape, where the
concept lives in a nested namespace) must be parsed as a type-constraint, not as
a non-type parameter of a qualified type.  Combined with a prior
declaration-context instantiation of the enclosing class, the mis-parse
truncated and cached the class, causing a downstream aggregate-init
out-of-bounds.  See doc/architectural/cpp-requires-expression-support.md.
